  "proposal": {
    "hypothesis": "Failures stem from two general defects: (1) rag_score uses raw overlap, so an untrusted/global-only high-overlap chunk outranks trusted in-scope evidence, and the prompt then treats the authoritative fact as unestablished (UNKNOWN) even when a trusted in-scope record exists; (2) tool_score uses raw overlap, so an unavailable or non-read-only tool can outrank the available read-only live registry, causing permanent-error dead-ends instead of falling back. Replacing rag_score and tool_score with a general authority/availability-aware ranking (trusted, scope_match, entity_match, available, read_only, freshness, overlap) will surface the authoritative evidence and the correct read-only tool without hardcoding any entity or answer.",
