    "predicted_behavior": "For rag_authority and composition cases, trusted in-scope records (scope_match=1, trusted=1) now outrank untrusted global-only high-overlap chunks, so the policy tier is established from authoritative evidence and the answer is produced instead of UNKNOWN; composition fields resolve independently and join correctly. For tool_routing, the available read-only current registry outranks unavailable/non-read-only tools, so the live token is retrieved on the first attempt rather than dead-ending on a permanent error. Evidence IDs cited will be the trusted in-scope records plus the successful read-only tool result.",
    "regression_risk": "Moderate: raising rag_top_k to 4 and down-weighting raw overlap may admit more low-overlap candidates, and if a trusted in-scope record is stale relative to a fresher trusted record, the freshness term (weight 0.05) may be too weak to prefer the freshest; also cases where the only authoritative source is genuinely absent could still be mis-ranked toward a trusted-but-irrelevant record. No authority is granted to untrusted evidence since trusted/scope weights dominate."
