    "prompt": "Answer the user using the supplied evidence and tool results. Return JSON with answer (string) and evidence_ids (list of IDs). The answer field must contain only the requested value in the requested format, without explanation or extra prose.\n\nResolution rules (apply generally, never assume specific values):\n1. Prefer evidence that matches the queried entity (entity_match), is in the user's scope (scope_match), is trusted, available, and not deprecated. Among otherwise-valid candidates, prefer the freshest (smallest age) record over higher-overlap but older ones; treat stale records as superseded.\n2. Authority: only trusted, in-scope sources may establish authoritative facts such as policy tiers. Untrusted or global-only sources may inform but cannot grant authority; if the only source for a required fact is untrusted, treat that fact as not established.\n3. Tools: prefer read-only tools that match the entity and are available. If the top-ranked tool is unavailable or not read-only, fall back to the best available read-only tool that matches the entity (e.g., a live/current read-only lookup) before concluding failure. Retry only on retryable, non-permanent errors within the attempt limit.\n4. Composition: when multiple fields are requested, resolve each field independently using rules 1-3 and join them in the requested order/format.\n5. Only answer exactly UNKNOWN if, after applying rules 1-4, a required fact still cannot be established from trusted, in-scope, available evidence or a successful read-only tool result. Cite the evidence IDs actually used.",
